meta {
  name: Parties - Update
  type: http
  seq: 41
}

put {
  url: {{lego_data_service_base_url}}/api/v1/parties/215
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  partyId: 215
}

params:query {
  ~allowDuplicateName: true
}

body:json {
  {
    "partyType": "P",
    "partyFirstName": "Sandbox",
    "partyLastName": "Test Seller (party endpoint check)",
    "partyEmail": "party-endpoint-check@example.com",
    "partyCity": "Raleigh",
    "partyCountry": "USA",
    "externalIdentities": [
      { "transactionPlatformName": "Bricklink", "externalPartyId": "sandbox-party-endpoint-check" }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Replaces an existing party's fields and answers 200 with the party (404 if it does not exist).

  - A field left out is cleared, so run "Parties - Find By Id" first and send back what should stay.
  - Kept when left out: partyType and externalIdentities.
  - When externalIdentities is sent, it is the full set the party has afterwards; [] removes them all.
  - 409 with code DUPLICATE_PARTY as for the add, against the other parties. The name is only checked
    when it changes.
  - Party 215 is the SANDBOX test seller; change the id for another party or environment.
}
